course: dictionary
lesson: 11705
title: Finding the meaning of auditor
level: primary-6
stars: 2
explain: An auditor is a person whose job is to check money records. You may not know the word, but the words around it give clues. «The auditor checked every number in the club's accounts.» Checked, numbers and accounts all tell you the job is about looking closely at money.
explain: «The auditor found one missing payment and wrote it in her report.» An auditor looks for mistakes, and a report tells you what was found. Ask yourself: what kind of person would fit here? Someone who checks money. Then swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
explain: Auditor is a noun, so you can add s for more: auditors. Two phrases help you too. An external auditor is a checker from outside the company, and the auditor's report is the written result of their check.
fact: An auditor is a person whose job is to check money records carefully, to make sure they are correct and honest.
fact: «The auditor's report» is the written result of the check.
fact: In the US, «auditor» can also mean a student who attends a class without taking it for marks.
fact: Context clues for «auditor» include words like checked, numbers, accounts, payment and report.
fact: A good check is to swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
exercise: «The company hired an auditor to check its accounts.» What is an auditor? | * A person who checks money records carefully | A teacher who marks spelling tests | A club member who makes the rules | A person who sells cakes at the school fair
exercise: «The auditor's report said the club's money was correct.» What does the auditor's report show? | * What the auditor found after checking | The price of new school books | A list of games for the playground | A map of the town
exercise: «The auditor found one missing payment.» Find and copy one word that tells you what the auditor was looking at. | one | found | * payment | auditor
test: Dad works for a bank as an auditor. What is his job? | Choosing the music for the bank's party | Painting the bank's walls | * Checking the bank's money records carefully | Ringing the bell at the start of each day
test: «At college, Sam is an auditor in the history class, so he does not take the test for marks.» In the US, what does auditor mean here? | A person who paints the classroom | A person who counts the students at lunch | * A student who attends a class without taking it for marks | A teacher who sets the test
exam: What is the main job of an auditor? | To lead the football team at break time | To paint the school walls in bright colours | To cook lunch for the whole class | * To check money records carefully to make sure they are correct
